 but there's no  doubt that  look it's dominating the news it is a  issue of utmost importance and  something's got to change  otherwise the whole effort in the House  of Representatives will lose credibility  I mean that's just obvious you've also  said that you said that President Trump  needs to address this issue what do you  want to hear from him at this point and  have you had any face-to-face meetings  with him would you like to well I think  there's a reception tonight over at the  White House and I'm sure in there but  are you invited I think so what would  you like to hear from the president  senator at this point in time well first  of all I'd like to go back to the the  latest debacle and that is that when the  Democrats rammed through Obamacare they  did it on a strict partisan basis we did  not include the Democrats and  negotiations on Obamacare the issue is  not going away it's imploding in Arizona  Obamacare is imploding we've got to go  back and address this issue on a  bipartisan basis and we can't wait until  people are without health care so and  now we got to move on to tax reform I  would say first thing you should do is  maybe bring that couple of trillion  dollars back to the United States at a  lower tax rate and then  work on infrastructure and you can sit  down together we've got to have some  bipartisanship around here otherwise  we're not going to get much done and  we've got a another government shutdown  looming as you know these are not good  times can I just go back to the Russian  interference in American elections you  have said in some cases this is worth  worse than any single terrorist attack  the dick cheney has said this morning  that in some quarters that would be  considered an act of war what is the  next shoe to drop what do you fear  coming out of this it's hard for me to  predict because I never would have  predicted the Chairman and the House  Intelligence Committee doing what he did  but I think that there is more  in